\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Forty days and forty nights
\par Thou wast fasting in the wild,
\par Forty days and forty nights
\par Tempted, and yet undefiled:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sunbeams scorching all the day,
\par Chilly dewdrops nightly shed,
\par Prowling beasts about Thy way,
\par Stones Thy pillow, earth Thy bed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let us Thy endurance share
\par And from earthly greed abstain;
\par With Thee watching unto prayer,
\par With Thee strong to suffer pain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And if Satan, vexing sore,
\par Flesh or spirit should assail,
\par Thou, his vanquisher before,
\par Grant we may not faint nor fail.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So shall we have peace divine;
\par Holier gladness ours shall be;
\par Round us too shall angels shine,
\par Such as ministered to Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

